    "problemStatement": "Suppose f(X,Y,Z)f(X, Y, Z)f(X,Y,Z) denotes the number of arrays AAA of length XXX such that:\n\n\n1≤Ai≤Y1 \\leq A_i \\leq Y1≤Ai​≤Y, for all (1≤i≤X)(1 \\leq i \\leq X)(1≤i≤X);\nThere are **at most** ZZZ values of iii (2≤i≤X)(2 \\leq i \\leq X)(2≤i≤X) such that Ai=Ai−1A_i=A_{i-1}Ai​=Ai−1​. In other words, for at most ZZZ indices, the element at a given index is equal to the previous element.\nYou are given an integer MMM and QQQ queries. The ithi^{th}ith query is of the form:\n\n\nNiN_iNi​ KiK_iKi​: Given integers NiN_iNi​ and KiK_iKi​, find the value f(Ni,M,Ki)f(N_i,M,K_i)f(Ni​,M,Ki​).\nSince output might be too large, print it modulo 998244353998244353998244353.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains a single integer MMM.\nThe second line of input contains an integer QQQ, the number of queries.\nEach of the next QQQ lines contains two integers NiN_iNi​ and KiK_iKi​.\n\n\nOutput Format\nPrint QQQ lines, where, in the ithi^{th}ith line, print a single integer f(Ni,M,Ki)f(N_i,M,K_i)f(Ni​,M,Ki​), the answer for ithi^{th}ith query modulo 998244353998244353998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "2≤M≤1032 \\leq M \\leq 10^32≤M≤103",
      "1≤Q≤1051 \\leq Q \\leq 10^51≤Q≤105",
      "2≤Ni≤1052 \\leq N_i \\leq 10^52≤Ni​≤105",
      "0≤Ki≤Ni−10 \\leq K_i \\leq N_i-10≤Ki​≤Ni​−1"
    ],
